      "snippet": {
        "text": "The present study had two primary objectives: (1) to investigate the frequency of usage and perceived usefulness of generative AI tools in schoolwork, including potential gender disparities in both usage and perceived usefulness; and (2) to examine how these usage patterns and perceived utility are associated with adolescents' EF and academic achievement. These objectives were pursued through two separate studies. Study 1 focused on a sample of young adolescents, comprising middle school students, while Study 2 involved older adolescents, including high school students. Given the early stage of research on AI, particularly in educational settings, no specific hypotheses were posited, and the study was approached as an exploratory correlational investigation. \n\n3 Study 1 3.1 Materials and methods",
