      "snippet": {
        "text": "Artificial Intelligence (AI) is profoundly reshaping educational assessment practices by automating routine evaluation tasks and delivering personalized learning experiences. With the rise of generative AI (GenAI) tools like ChatGPT, assessments can now offer real-time feedback and adapt to individual learner profiles (Ansari et al., 2024;Heil et al., 2025). However, current AI-based systems often emphasize lower-level cognitive skills, such as factual recall and procedural tasks, rather than fostering higher-order thinking abilities such as analysis, synthesis, and critical reasoning (Foung et al., 2024;Roll & Wylie, 2016). Addressing these limitations is crucial for developing AI tools that support deeper learning. \n\nSocratic questioning, a pedagogical method rooted in structured inquiry and dialogue, offers a framework for cultivating higher-order thinking. Research has demonstrated that engaging with Socratic dialogue enhances students' ability to question assumptions, articulate reasoning, and reflect on their understanding (Chin & Osborne, 2008). Yet, traditional methods of implementing Socratic dialogue require extensive instructor involvement, limiting scalability. GenAI platforms integrating Socratic questioning hold promise for addressing this challenge by delivering scalable and adaptive assessments (Authors, 2024). \n\nLearner engagement-cognitive, emotional, and behavioral-plays a critical role in the successful use of AI tools (Heung & Chiu, 2025). Design features and User Experiences (UX) significantly influence the depth and quality of learner interaction (Chi & Wylie, 2014;D'Mello & Graesser, 2023;Sajja et al., 2025). Students' varying levels of AI literacy, prior experience, and confidence further impact how they engage with these tools (Guettala et al., 2024). So far though, existing studies report mixed findings on GenAI's impact on learning outcomes, which requires further empirical research (Bauer et al., 2025). \n\nThis study introduces Socratic Mind, a novel GenAI-powered assessment tool that employs dynamic Socratic questioning through adaptive interactions.",
