      "snippet": {
        "text": "In the context of tutoring systems, Artificial Intelligence encompasses the algorithms and computational models that enable these technologies to deliver personalized and adaptive learning experiences [5], [13]. Early tutoring systems relied on foundational techniques, such as concept trees and student models, to map student progress and adapt instruction based on predefined rules [25]- [27]. Subsequent advancements introduced Bayesian Knowledge Tracing, which improved predictive capabilities, allowing systems to adjust instructional content dynamically based on real-time student performance [22]. \n\nModern tutoring systems integrate advanced AI models, such as ChatGPT and other large language models, to create interactive, conversational learning experiences [23], [24]. These models facilitate real-time feedback and adaptive interactions, tailoring the learning process to individual student needs. This evolution has transformed tutoring systems into responsive, AI-driven tools that emulate many qualities of human tutors, offering highly adaptive and personalized educational experiences [12].",
